            },
            {
              "document_hash": "0b686ce3baeceade91a82826fc80957c3ba46062679b3d0eba88b20fd25a2f84",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0b686ce3baec-0001-0009"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 13,
                "start": 13
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Saada argues that determining whether a grave risk of harm exists must include consideration of any ameliorative measures that are available."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Saada",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0b686ce3baeceade91a82826fc80957c3ba46062679b3d0eba88b20fd25a2f84",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0b686ce3baec-0001-0009"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 13,
                "start": 13
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Saada, he contends that this requirement is implicit in the Hague Convention\u2019s command that the court determine whether a grave risk of harm exists."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Saada",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0b686ce3baeceade91a82826fc80957c3ba46062679b3d0eba88b20fd25a2f84",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0b686ce3baec-0001-0010"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 14,
                "start": 14
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Saada, saada points to the practice of other signatory countries, such as the United Kingdom, to support the view that consideration of ameliorative measures is required."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Saada\u2019s Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Karen R. King",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "6779fe44e8632209c327ae74ac88c5dc5cee939ba4fb9afebd2e8324e1fa2121",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-6779fe44e863-0000-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 5,
                "start": 5
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Karen R. King, Ms. King states that once the grave\u2011risk exception is met, the Hague Convention does not bind a court to return the child."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. King",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "6779fe44e8632209c327ae74ac88c5dc5cee939ba4fb9afebd2e8324e1fa2121",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-6779fe44e863-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 26,
                "start": 26
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Ms. King argues that after a finding of grave risk, courts have discretion either to deny the petition for return or to grant it subject to ameliorative measures."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. King",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "6779fe44e8632209c327ae74ac88c5dc5cee939ba4fb9afebd2e8324e1fa2121",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-6779fe44e863-0003-0007"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 82,
                "start": 82
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. King, this is the first case in which a mother has satisfied the high evidentiary standard for the grave\u2011risk exception."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Golan (via Ms. King) Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
